-add benchmark launches accumulate into the same un-zeroed C32 buffer -> values exceed fp16 max on cast -> inf/nan. GEMM index math and tl.dot layout are correct; the bug is purely the autotune+atomic-without-reset interaction.\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"M\": 4, \"uuid\": \"f439da26\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}, {\"M\": 48, \"uuid\": \"59ca23f5\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}, {\"M\": 64, \"uuid\": \"67d4c8f3\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}, {\"M\": 128, \"uuid\": \"29ebd771\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}, {\"M\": 240, \"uuid\": \"e7c939ae\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"reject-invalid-fix-next\", \"decision_reason\": \"Split-K structure is sound but invalid: the autotuner re-launches the atomic kernel during benchmarking with no reset_to_zero, overflowing C32 -> non-finite. Fix in c003 by adding reset_to_zero=['C32'] so every benchmarked launch (and the reset before the real launch) starts from a zeroed buffer. Does not falsify H3 (occupancy hypothesis still untested).\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 2, \"skill_usage\": \"none (sm_80 outside KernelWiki scope)\"}","originalFile":"{\"candidate_id\": \"c001\", \"parent_id\": null, \"source_sha256\": \"79b1d17b6528c24ef8ffccf506c951c88d51e621d565965d074296fdd9447b34\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T00:00:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"A plain autotuned NT GEMM (fp32 accum, no split-K) is correct but under-occupies 108 SMs for skinny M, losing to cuBLAS on M=4/48/64.\", \"change_from_parent\": \"first implementation: grouped-along-M NT GEMM, fp32 acc, fp16 store, autotune key=['M'], no split-K\", \"config\": {\"BLOCK_M\": \"autotuned{16,32,64}\", \"BLOCK_N\": \"autotuned{64,128,256}\", \"BLOCK_K\": \"autotuned{32,64}\", \"SPLIT_K\": 1, \"num_warps\": \"4|8\", \"num_stages\": \"3|4\", \"GROUP_SIZE_M\": 8, \"reduction\": \"non