_M\": \"autotuned{16,64,128,256}\", \"BLOCK_N\": \"autotuned{32,64,128}\", \"BLOCK_K\": 64, \"SPLIT_K\": \"autotuned{2,4,8,16}\", \"num_warps\": \"4|8\", \"num_stages\": 3, \"GROUP_SIZE_M\": null, \"reduction\": \"atomic\", \"adaptive\": true}, \"validation\": {\"static_checklist_passed\": true, \"all_workloads_correct\": false, \"tolerance_notes\": \"INVALID: 0/5 passed, all 'C: non-finite output mismatch'. Root cause: @triton.autotune benchmarks each of 12 configs with warmup+rep launches, but reset_to_zero was NOT set, so the ~hundreds of atomic-add benchmark launches accumulate into the same un-zeroed C32 buffer -> values exceed fp16 max on cast -> inf/nan. GEMM index math and tl.dot layout are correct; the bug is purely the autotune+atomic-without-reset interaction.\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"M\": 4, \"uuid\": \"f439da26\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}, {\"M\": 48, \"uuid\": \"59ca23f5\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}, {\"M\": 64, \"uuid\": \"67d4c8f3\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}, {\"M\": 128, \"uuid\": \"29ebd771\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}, {\"M\": 240, \"uuid\": \"e7c939ae\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null, \"latency_us\": null}], \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"reject-invalid-fix-next\", \"decision_reason\": \"Split-K structure is sound but invalid: the autotuner re-launches the atomic kernel during benchmarking with no reset_to_zero, overflowing C32 -> non-finite. Fix in c003 by adding reset_to_zero=['C32'] so every benchmarked launch (and the reset before the real launch) starts from a zeroed buffer. Does not falsify H3 (occupancy hypothesis still untested).\", \"cumulative_evaluations\": 2, \"skill_usage\": \"none (sm_80 outside KernelWiki scope)\"}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":2,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":[" {\"candidate_id\": \"c001\", \"parent_id\": null, \"source_sha256\": \"79